      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for these. It's a good start but it's still a bit thin. I need these comments to carry more weight so they don't get flagged as \"low impact\" by the department head. \n\nCan you expand on those specific points? Especially the part about the long-range dependencies and the sparse-masking. Make it more detailed and intellectually heavy so it really lands like a senior expert's critique. \n\nJust a reminder—don't just throw in buzzwords for the sake of it. If the points feel fake or just padded with critical terms without actual substance, it'll look bad on my end. Make sure the logic is actually there.",
