      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The assertion that the sliding window mechanism successfully preserves long-range dependencies warrants significant scrutiny, as the inherent truncation of context within a fixed window presents a fundamental theoretical limitation that the authors fail to adequately address. Specifically, the paper lacks a formal analysis demonstrating how the global token set mitigates the information decay typically associated with localized attention patterns, rendering the claim potentially contradictory to established complexity theory. Moreover, the sparse-masking technique's robustness is insufficiently explored; the authors must provide a more detailed ablation study to prove that the observed performance gains are not merely artifacts of the specific GLUE benchmarks used, highlighting a critical oversight in generalizability.",
